title: 'pallet-validator-collators: drop validators that author no blocks'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |-
    `pallet-validator-collators` can stop returning validators that do not run a collator node.

    Governance sets the rule with the new `set_drop_rule` call. There is no rule by default, so
    nobody is dropped.

    The pallet checks the validators when a new set arrives or the cap changes. A validator that
    missed at least `min_missed_turns` of its own Aura turns without authoring a block is not
    returned for one era. Each further drop doubles that time, up to a limit the rule sets. A
    floor keeps a minimum number of validators.

    Missed turns are counted in blocks, so time when the chain is halted does not count.

    New storage items: `CurrentDropRule`, `LastActivity` and `Dropped`. No migration.

    `pallet_validator_collators::Config` changes:
    - It now requires `pallet_session::Config` with `ValidatorId = AccountId`.
    - New item `MaxBlocksPerSlot`: the most blocks the chain can build in one Aura slot. Asset
      Hub Westend and People Westend set it.
crates:
- name: pallet-validator-collators
  bump: major
- name: asset-hub-westend-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: people-westend-runtime
  bump: minor
- name: pallet-validator-set-announcer
  bump: none
- name: people-westend-integration-tests
  bump: none
- name: cumulus-zombienet-sdk-tests
  bump: none
